# Main UI screens recognition

Player-facing screens, windows, overlays, HUD layout, and navigation follow `.cursor/MAIN_UI_SCREENS_SPECIFICATION.md`.

When that work is in scope:

1. Use skill `rimworld-go-ui-screens` (canonical playbook: `.cursor/skills/rimworld-go-ui-screens/SKILL.md`).
2. Load only the spec sections that skill names for the screen — not the whole file by default.
3. Also use `.cursor/RIMWORLD_GO_UI_UX_IMPLEMENTATION_CHECKLIST.md` for ordered backlog/acceptance.
4. Screens consume read models and emit typed commands; they never mutate domain state.
5. Honor §58 (screen vs window vs overlay) and Wave UI-0 before later-wave screens.
6. Update matching screen-wave and DoD checkboxes (`[x]` / `[-]` / `[!]`).

Skip the spec for headless simulation-only tasks with no screen.
